---
import { bookingUrl, CTA_LABEL } from '../config';
import ArrowUpRight from './ArrowUpRight.astro';
interface Props { title?: string; emphasis?: string; placement?: string; }
const { title = 'Technology should make the business', emphasis = 'easier to run.', placement = 'closing' } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="conversation section-dark" aria-labelledby="conversation-title">
  <div class="shell conversation-layout">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Let’s talk</p><h2 id="conversation-title" class="display">{title}<br /><em>{emphasis}</em></h2></div>
    <div class="conversation-copy"><p>If it isn’t, let’s find out why and what to do about it.</p><p>You don’t need to have the problem neatly framed. In fact, that’s often the point.</p><a class="button button--primary" href={bookingUrl(placement)}>{CTA_LABEL} <ArrowUpRight /></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
